==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|wërden}}, from {{inh|de|goh|werdan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*werþan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*werþaną}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nl|worden}}, {{cog|sv|varda}}, {{cog|nn|verta}}, obsolete {{cog|en|worth||to become}} and also with {{cog|la|vertere||to turn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈveːrdən/|[ˈveːɐ̯.dn̩]|[ˈvɛɐ̯-]|[ʋ-]|[-dən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-werden.ogg|audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|<irreg.sein>}}

# {{lb|de|auxiliary|with an infinitive|past participle {{m|de|geworden}}}} [[will]]; to be going (to do something); {{non-gloss definition|forms the future tense}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''werde''' nach Hause gehen.|I '''will''' go home.}}
# {{lb|de|auxiliary|with a past participle|past participle {{m|de|worden}}}} to be done; {{non-gloss definition|forms the passive voice}}
#: {{ux|de|Das Buch '''wird''' gerade gelesen.|q=present tense|The book '''is''' being read.}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''wurde''' in Europa geboren.|q=preterite tense|I '''was''' born in Europe.}}
#: {{ux|de|Er war geschlagen '''worden'''.|q=past perfect tense|He had '''been''' beaten.}}
# {{lb|de|copulative|past participle {{m|de|geworden}}}} to [[become]]; to [[get]]; to [[grow]]; to [[turn]]
#: {{ux|de|Es '''wird''' heißer.|It's '''getting''' hotter.}}
# {{lb|de|with a dative object and certain adjectives}} to begin or come to [[feel]] or [[experience]] (a condition)
#:'''Usage:''' In this sense '''werden''' is always conjugated in the third person singular and takes a dative noun. The impersonal subject '''es''' may be present, but is often taken as implied. (See the usage note for a similar meaning of {{m|de|sein}}.)
#: {{uxi|de|Wird dir kalt?|Are you getting cold?}}
#: {{uxi|de|Den Kindern wird langweilig.|The children are getting bored.}}
#: {{ux|de|Von Mayonnaise wird mir schlecht.|Mayonnaise makes me sick. (Literally: From mayonnaise I become sick.)}}
# {{lb|de|copulative|colloquial}} to [[be]], to [[happen]], to [[occur]] (in the future)
#: {{ux|de|Wir '''werden''' zusammen glücklich.|We ''will be'' happy together.}}
#: {{ux|de|Was wird aus mir?|What will become of me?}}
# {{lb|de|colloquial}} to be going to work
#: {{ux|de|Das wird so nichts.|It will not work like that.}}
#: {{syn|de|klappen|funktionieren}}

